    {
      "id": "f51c3085-9cd6-4bc4-b2ff-a72188f3bb72",
      "name": "Overview Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -464,
        -288
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 440,
        "height": 1000,
        "content": "## Monitor Japanese business partners for registry changes with gBizINFO and Gemini\n\n### How it works\nA supplier that quietly renames, relocates or dissolves can invalidate your contracts and invoices. Every week this template reads your partner list from Google Sheets and looks each corporate number up in gBizINFO, Japan's official corporate registry API. A Code node diffs the live registry against the stored snapshot, and only partners with real changes go to a Basic LLM Chain with Google Gemini, which rates how material the change is and recommends an action. The snapshot is upserted by corporate number so each change is reported once, then a Switch escalates: material changes raise a Slack alert plus a credit-review email draft, paperwork-level changes are notified, cosmetic ones are logged only.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect Google Sheets, Google Gemini (PaLM) API, Gmail and Slack.\n2. Get a free gBizINFO API token and store it as a Header Auth credential.\n3. Add a Partners sheet with Corporate Number, Company Name, Last Name and Last Address.\n\n### Customization tips\nAdd more registry fields to the diff, or check daily for critical suppliers."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
